From c1eccde54fa060d0d01973e85380827ede44913d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:22:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: use common 80-byte FoE representation

Model the FoE table with a common 80-byte physical stride across the
supported EcoNet and Airoha generations. Keep the generation-specific
information blocks explicit in soc_data and encode FoE v1 entries as
32-bit hardware words so EN751221 big-endian and EN7528 little-endian
use the same bit layout.

Restore TB_ENTRY_SIZE after the EN7523 stock register profile so the
hardware stays in the SDK default 80-byte mode. Fold generation-1 PPE
ownership state into struct airoha_ppe, remove the duplicate EcoNet FoE
structures, and use the 0x40 meter/accounting word on EN7581/AN7583.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c      |   9 +-
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h      | 191 +++---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c      | 603 ++++++++----------
 .../net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe_debugfs.c  | 220 ++++---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_regs.h     |  25 -
 5 files changed, 509 insertions(+), 539 deletions(-)

